<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="230b" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Keyless proof (D13): the BFF proves one managed-identity call per stamp service to H13 (401/403 fails acceptance, never a skip), L2 proves key auth is off on every resource, and a build-time guard stops key credentials coming back</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T230 part 2 (D13)</phase>
    <gate>after 230a</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New BFF endpoint (BFF §10), auth (app role, token audience), H3/H13 handler changes, ArchTest.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-relevant: a new authenticated BFF surface and the forcing function for ADR-028 keyless stamps.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>BFF hot path + skill/constraints docs (main session).</parallel-reason>
    <tags>provisioning, provisioning-handler, l2-controlplane, bff-api, auth, model1-dedicated, testing</tags>
    <deps>230a, 244, 246</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make "the stamp is keyless" something H13 proves on every run, not something the templates merely intend.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (BFF, L2 control plane, Entra app roles).</role>

  <goal>
    D13: every BFF call to the customer's Azure services uses the stamp UAMI and key auth is disabled where Azure allows
    it. After this task H13 refuses Ready unless (a) the BFF, with its own identity, made one real call to each stamp
    service and none was refused, and (b) ARM shows key/local auth disabled on each resource and no key setting on either
    slot. The OpenAI result is the ADR-028 E-2 measurement on a `kind: OpenAI` account (T235 retires or extends E-2 from it).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Mapped 2026-10-06 (SESSION 40 exploration):
      - No H13 check calls a stamp service as the stamp UAMI; only L2 can call AI Search with its own identity (L2 has no
        data-plane role on Service Bus, OpenAI, Document Intelligence, Storage, Redis, Content Safety or Cosmos). The stamp
        UAMI holds the needed roles (bff-runtime-rbac.bicep, openai/doc-intelligence/content-safety Cognitive Services
        User, storage Blob Data Contributor, Cosmos Data Contributor, Redis access policy) but is usable only inside the
        BFF (ADR-028: Kudu has no IDENTITY_ENDPOINT). So the per-service proof must run in the BFF.
      - BFF credential paths: Service Bus ServiceBusClientFactory:72-95; AI Search SearchClientFactory:61-84 (and a
        key-only CustomerOwned path in KnowledgeDeploymentService:318-325, 450-458); OpenAI AiModule:125-138 +
        OpenAiClient:91-113; Document Intelligence TextExtractorService:105-127; Redis CacheModule (MI only when Endpoint
        set); Blob SessionFileBlobStore:225; Cosmos AiPersistenceModule:101; Content Safety ContentSafetyAuthHandler:84-103.
        Prompt Shield (PromptShieldService:145-157) and groundedness (GroundednessCheckService:137-155) fail OPEN on 401/403
        with no distinct auth outcome.
      - E2EValidationRunner requests an L2 token for `{bff host}/.default` (:481-482) but the BFF expects
        `api://{appId}`; token failure or 401/403 makes its sample checks SKIP (:496-510, :673-682), and skips do not fail
        H13 — so they never run for real.
      - ADR-028 E-2 (:396-421): MI 401 on the shared dev `kind=AIServices` account; stamps deploy `kind: OpenAI` with local
        auth disabled — T230's call is the first measurement.
      - The real per-service measurement happens on the first live run (T186); this task builds and tests the mechanism.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/** (endpoint + module per bff-extensions.md; the credential factories above; Services/Ai/Safety)</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/** (H3: BFF app registration) and Handlers/E2EAcceptance/** (H13, E2EValidationRunner)</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/modules/*.bicep (disableLocalAuth / allowSharedKeyAccess / accessKeysAuthentication)</file>
      <file>tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/** (new key-credential ratchet)</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md (E-2); .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="BFF §10">Placement justification, publish size against a fresh master build (same zip tool, short paths, file counts), CVE check, tests; endpoint mapped via a Map{Feature}Endpoints extension; unconditional registration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth">The diagnostics endpoint accepts only an app-only token for the stamp's BFF audience carrying a dedicated app role that only the L2 Worker identity is assigned (H3 creates the role + assignment); it returns per-service status codes and timings only — no data, no secrets, no exception text beyond a code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="fail-closed">A 401/403 from any service, a missing service configuration, or an unreachable endpoint fails H13 (QuarantineRequired for auth, Resumable for transient); never a skip. The sample-workload checks' auth skip goes the same way.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D13">No key fallback is added; the ArchTest pins the existing "key if configured, else MI" sites (shared dev env) so a new key credential fails the build.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">No live call, role assignment or deployment in this task — the live measurement is T186's; ask before anything live.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">BFF: authenticated keyless-diagnostics endpoint — one minimal call per service with the injected credentials (Service Bus, AI Search, OpenAI chat + embeddings, Document Intelligence, Blob, Redis, Cosmos, Content Safety Prompt Shield + groundedness); Content Safety's fail-open records a distinct auth outcome; tests; §10 measurements.</step>
    <step order="2">H3: app role on the customer's BFF app registration + assignment to the L2 Worker identity; tests.</step>
    <step order="3">H13: runner token audience `api://{appId}`; call the diagnostics endpoint; auth failures fail; ARM local-auth-off + no-key-setting check; tests.</step>
    <step order="4">ArchTest key-credential ratchet; decide KnowledgeDeploymentService's key-only path (needed → MI, else remove).</step>
    <step order="5">Docs: guide H13 row + §3.2 keyless, constraints, ADR-028 E-2 note (measurement pending T186), CHANGELOG; T186 checklist item.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify (BFF + ControlPlane tests, ArchTests, builds 0 warnings, publish size); Step 9.5; close.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The endpoint refuses an anonymous call, a user token, and an app token without the role (401/403); with the role it returns one result per service; a service returning 401/403 is reported as refused, never as healthy.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H13 fails (QuarantineRequired) when the endpoint reports any service refused or a resource has local/key auth enabled or a slot carries a key setting; passes when all are proved; never skips on auth.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H3 creates the app role and assigns it to the L2 Worker identity idempotently.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The ArchTest fails when a new AzureKeyCredential / ApiKeyCredential / key-header site is added outside the pinned list.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish delta reported against a fresh master build; no new HIGH CVE; all suites green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A service has no minimal call that is free of side effects or cost (e.g. groundedness/Prompt Shield billing) — record the cost; ask if it is material.</trigger>
    <trigger>Adding the app role needs a permission the H3 identity does not hold.</trigger>
    <trigger>ADR conflict (e.g. ADR-008 endpoint filters, ADR-028 MUSTs) → CLAUDE.md §6.5.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <notes/>
</task>
